From 3f1bf074f5ba6df932b0e72f859377feeceb461e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 14:41:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 01/42] multitenant: scaffold per-tenant Bifrost runtime
 registry

Wraps the unchanged core/bifrost runtime in a tenant-keyed Manager that
lazy-loads each tenant on first Acquire, refcounts in-flight Handles to
defer eviction, and runs an LRU policy when MaxActiveRuntimes is set.

Phase 2 of the enterprise multi-tenant fork plan: validates that we can
run N independent Bifrost worlds in one process without touching
core/bifrost.go.

- tenant.go     TenantID, TenantLoader callback
- runtime.go    runtimeEntry (initOnce/refCount/lastUsed), Handle
- manager.go    Manager.Acquire, Evict, Shutdown; LRU + refcount-aware eviction
- resolver.go   VKResolver interface, MemoryVKResolver, TTL-cached wrapper
- account.go    StaticAccount: tenant-scoped schemas.Account impl for fixtures

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
